/*  FUNCTION NAME:      MAZELAM_ELEV
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Stock Mazelam for MAZE: treats Cost as elevation. Uphill steps cost 1 + 2x the rise; downhill steps cost 1 + 0.5x the drop (negative); flat steps cost 1.*/
/*  RETURNS:            array of step costs (numbers): 1 + 2x rise uphill, 1 + 0.5x drop downhill, 1 flat
    PARAMETERS:
        costFrom        (Required) Elevation at source cell.
        costTo          (Required) Elevation at destination cell.
        cellFrom        (Required) A1 address of source cell (e.g. "C3"). (Unused by this Mazelam.)
        cellTo          (Required) A1 address of destination cell (e.g. "D4"). (Unused.)
        distFrom        (Required) Cumulative cost to reach source. (Unused.)
        dirDelta        (Required) This step's direction. (Unused.)
        prevDir         (Required) Previous direction. (Unused.)
    EXAMPLE:            =MAZE("A1", elevationMap, , , , , , MAZELAM_ELEV) -> Distance grid where uphill is penalised 2x and downhill is rewarded 0.5x
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-05-20  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-05-27  Claude      Signature changed: cellFrom/cellTo (A1 strings) replace rowFrom/colFrom/rowTo/colTo
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
MAZELAM_ELEV = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [costFrom],
    [costTo],
    [cellFrom],
    [cellTo],
    [distFrom],
    [dirDelta],
    [prevDir],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        delta, costTo - costFrom,
        result, 1 + IF(delta > 0, delta * 2, delta * 0.5),
        result
)
);
